# The Ink Room uses two env files — one per app:
#
#   backend/.env         ← copy from backend/.env.example   (database, storage, secrets)
#   frontend/.env.local  ← copy from frontend/.env.example  (site URL, API URL, image host)
#
# Summary of every variable:
#
# backend/.env
#   NODE_ENV, PORT                 Runtime + port of the Express API (default 4000)
#   FRONTEND_ORIGIN                Public origin of the site; used for CORS + CSRF origin checks
#   DATABASE_URL                   Supabase pooled connection (port 6543, ?pgbouncer=true)
#   DIRECT_URL                     Supabase direct connection (port 5432) for migrations
#   STORAGE_DRIVER                 "supabase" (default) or "local" (offline development only)
#   SUPABASE_URL                   https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY      SERVER ONLY. Never expose to the browser.
#   SUPABASE_STORAGE_BUCKET        Bucket for portfolio photos (created automatically, public read)
#   LOCAL_UPLOAD_DIR, PUBLIC_API_URL   Only for STORAGE_DRIVER=local
#   MAX_UPLOAD_MB                  Upload limit for original photos (default 15)
#   SESSION_TTL_HOURS              Admin session lifetime (default 168 = 7 days)
#   TRUST_PROXY                    Proxy hops in front of the API (1 behind the Next.js proxy)
#   FRONTEND_REVALIDATE_URL        http(s)://<site>/api/revalidate
#   REVALIDATE_SECRET              Shared with the frontend; refreshes pages after edits
#
# frontend/.env.local
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL           Canonical public URL of the site
#   BACKEND_URL                    Where the Express API runs (server-side only)
#   MEDIA_ORIGIN                   Your Supabase project URL, allowed for image optimisation
#   IMAGES_ALLOW_LOCAL             1 only with STORAGE_DRIVER=local
#   REVALIDATE_SECRET              Same value as in backend/.env
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_MAX_UPLOAD_MB      Optional; keep in sync with MAX_UPLOAD_MB (default 15)
